# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Emir Kocer et al. (2022). Neural Network Potentials: A Concise Overview of Methods.
#   Annual Review of Physical Chemistry. doi:10.1146/annurev-physchem-082720-034254  arXiv:2107.03727v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2107.03727v1 (sha256 8992c2425f7cdc48...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 24 (Overview/taxonomy). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The article is a review in
# the Annual Review of Physical Chemistry of neural network potentials:
# predefined-descriptor methods (high-dimensional neural network
# potentials of the second to fourth generation and others) and
# learnable-descriptor message-passing methods (DTNN, SchNet, HIP-NN,
# AIMNet and others). It reports no training run of its own. Read from
# the arXiv preprint (v1).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
